IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `il38-nouns`
IMPORT `il38-rules`

-- Courts Law [Consolidated Version], 5744-1984, the provisions in scope: THE SEAT LAYER. Row IL-38.
--
-- SEAT: a person who may be chosen a Supreme Court judge or a public representative on the committee, and a judge whose term the committee is asked to end.
-- The committee, the Minister, the Knesset and the Court have no seat. Each question takes plain facts the person can state and calls the rule already encoded in il38-rules.l4; no rule is restated.
-- The text from the 26th Knesset is the one the questions apply, except where the question says otherwise.

§ `The questions of a candidate and of a judge`

@export Am I eligible to be chosen a Supreme Court judge, or a public representative on the committee (s 2, s 6C(a))?
GIVEN `how many years I served as a judge of a district court` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many years have you served as a judge of a district court?
      `how many years I have been on the Bar's register, or entitled to be, practising as a lawyer, as a judge or legal officer of the State, or teaching law` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many years in all have you been registered, or entitled to be registered, in the Bar's register and practising as a lawyer, in a judicial or other legal post in the State's service the regulations list, or teaching law at a university?
      `how many of those years were in Israel` IS A NUMBER @desc Of those years, how many were in Israel?
      `I am a distinguished jurist` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you recognised as a distinguished jurist (a jurist of outstanding standing)?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`am I eligible` MEANS
    `the person is eligible to be a Supreme Court judge` (`A candidate for the Supreme Court` OF `how many years I served as a judge of a district court`, `how many years I have been on the Bar's register, or entitled to be, practising as a lawyer, as a judge or legal officer of the State, or teaching law`, `how many of those years were in Israel`, `I am a distinguished jurist`)

@export Can I be chosen a Supreme Court judge, having been Attorney General or State Attorney (s 2A(a))?
GIVEN `I served as Attorney General or State Attorney` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Have you served as Attorney General or as State Attorney?
      `whole months since my term ended` IS A NUMBER @desc How many whole months have passed since that term ended?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`am I past the cooling-off` MEANS
    `the cooling-off of 18 months is over` `I served as Attorney General or State Attorney` `whole months since my term ended`

@export Is the committee's choice of me as a Supreme Court judge valid at my age, on the votes it got (s 2A(b), from the 26th Knesset)?
GIVEN `my age in whole years` IS A NUMBER @desc How many whole years old are you (not yet 55 means younger than 55)?
      `I was appointed to the Supreme Court before the 26th Knesset's term began` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you appointed a Supreme Court judge before the first day of the 26th Knesset's term?
      `members serving on the committee` IS A NUMBER @desc How many members were serving on the committee when it voted?
      `members who voted for me` IS A NUMBER @desc How many members voted for you?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`does my age need every serving member` MEANS
    `the choice of a Supreme Court judge meets section 2A(b)` `the text from the 26th Knesset` `my age in whole years` `I was appointed to the Supreme Court before the 26th Knesset's term began` `members serving on the committee` `members who voted for me`

@export Did the committee follow the procedure when it ended my term (s 14(b))?
GIVEN `I was allowed to read the material before the committee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you allowed to read the material before the committee or its sub-committee?
      `I was given the opportunity to be heard` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you given the opportunity to state your case to the committee or its sub-committee?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`did the committee follow the procedure` MEANS
    `the committee followed section 14(b)` `I was allowed to read the material before the committee` `I was given the opportunity to be heard`
